meta {
  name: 0 Happy Path
}

docs {
  # Scenario 0 — Happy Path (2.1a, 2.2a, 3.1a/b)

  The whole pipeline, end to end: a device is registered at dispatch, delivers a
  reading, and the reading lands in Strata.Core attributed to the right Member — with
  its business event captured in the transactional outbox. Then the provider re-sends
  the same reading and NOTHING duplicates. Run in order; nothing to fill in (request 1
  generates a fresh device id and provider reading id per run, so it repeats forever).

  1. Register the device to Member m-1 (the demo cast's Morgan Lee)
  2. Deliver a weight reading from that device — captured, 202
  3. Run the pipeline — the reading is validated, attributed to m-1, and persisted
  4. The provider re-sends the SAME reading (same reading_id, new delivery) — 202 again
  5. Run the pipeline — the duplicate is recognised and acknowledged, nothing written

  Verify (optional):
  psql: SELECT user_id, weight_kg, weight_lbs, suspect, provider_reading_id
        FROM weight_readings ORDER BY created_at DESC LIMIT 3;
  — exactly ONE row for this run's provider_reading_id, user m-1, suspect false,
  both unit systems exactly as sent.
  psql: SELECT event_type, published_at, payload->>'reading_row_id' FROM readings_outbox_events
        ORDER BY created_at DESC LIMIT 3;
  — exactly one reading.received event for it, published_at NULL (the Elevate relay
  is gated on).
}
